# 8. Supabase Row Level Security (RLS)

Enable RLS on both new tables.

The implementation must follow the existing RevOS authentication and authorization model.

### Business Challenge permissions

- Public or unauthenticated users may read active Business Challenges only if this is consistent with the existing public-content access strategy.
- Authorized CMS administrators may read all Business Challenges.
- Authorized CMS administrators may create Business Challenges.
- Authorized CMS administrators may update Business Challenges.
- Unauthorized users must not create, modify, or delete Business Challenges.

### Article association permissions

- Public users must not be allowed to modify article-to-challenge relationships.
- Authorized CMS administrators must be able to read and manage associations.
- If published article associations are exposed publicly in the future, public read access must be limited to associations belonging to published Insight articles and active Business Challenges.

Do not use a simple authenticated-user check if the existing application has administrator roles or permission-based authorization.

Reuse the existing role or permission mechanism.

Do not expose the Supabase service-role key in frontend code.

Do not disable RLS to make the implementation work.

If a SECURITY DEFINER RPC function is needed, implement it carefully:

- Set a fixed and safe search path.
- Verify the caller's identity.
- Verify the caller's CMS administrator permissions.
- Validate all supplied IDs.
- Restrict execution permissions to appropriate roles.
- Do not allow unauthorized users to bypass RLS.

